# Git hooks are shell scripts and MUST check out with LF endings.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is true on the Windows checkouts this repo runs from, which
# would otherwise give `.githooks/pre-push` a CRLF shebang. The kernel then
# reads the interpreter as `/bin/sh\r` and the hook fails with "bad
# interpreter" on macOS and Linux -- and a pre-push hook that cannot execute
# makes git ABORT THE PUSH rather than skip the hook.
#
# scripts/install-git-hooks.mjs also normalises to LF when it writes, so the
# guard survives a checkout that ignores this file. Both are deliberate: this
# rule fixes the working copy, the installer fixes what actually runs.
.githooks/** text eol=lf
